
=== system audio without a sound server (linux-audio-alsa-fallback) ===
  ok   reads PipeWire's own wpctl when pactl is absent
  ok   falls through a pactl with no server to the next stack
  ok   reads the ALSA mixer when neither PulseAudio nor PipeWire is present
  ok   measures no muted time when no sound stack answers

=== system audio native output locale ===
  ok   linux-system-audio-locale: retains French muted=true
  ok   linux-system-audio-locale: retains French muted=false
  ok   linux-system-audio-locale: retains German muted=true
  ok   linux-system-audio-locale: retains German muted=false

=== system metrics: reading the machine ===
  ok   records the battery it was told
  ok   keeps the lowest and highest charge of the day
  ok   does not sample again before the interval has passed
  ok   starts a fresh row on a new day

=== system metrics: awake, locked, asleep ===
  ok   counts the time between samples as awake
  ok   counts it as locked when the session was locked
  ok   calls a long gap sleep rather than use
  ok   reports the lock and the unlock between two answers, never from 'cannot tell'

=== system metrics: network changes ===
  ok   counts a change of network
  ok   does not count a change to or from 'cannot tell'
  ok   reads the wireless interface with no tool on the PATH (wireless-without-awk)
  ok   leaves the readings it cannot make at zero

=== system metrics: owned restart hydration ===
  ok   unbound-recovery: merges first binding without losing clocks or queued transitions
  ok   hydrates the owned cumulative row before its first sample
  ok   seeds an acknowledged absent row without invented history
  ok   refuses unread history and retries without a writable zero day
  ok   same database and device rebinding retains the accumulated day
  ok   isolates changed database or device owned-b/device-a
  ok   isolates changed database or device owned-a/device-b
  ok   hydrates a new date and partitions its own elapsed sample clock
  ok   folds new battery readings into the persisted extrema and sum
  ok   a throwing loader cannot publish a destructive zero day
  ok   reset clears the owned loader as well as the sampling state

=== capture calendar ownership ===
  ok   retires closed sources only after their complete exact prefix is acknowledged

=== system-event-capture-policy ===
  ok   refuses missing or malformed authority before sensor acquisition
  ok   samples the exact policy once per due observation without gating aggregates

=== ngram walker: the nine families ===
  ok   produces tokens of every length from one to seven
  ok   records words and word pairs
  ok   keeps the last word even though the stream ends mid-sentence

=== ngram walker: what must not become a sequence ===
  ok   keeps long-gap characters but excludes their delay from n-gram timing
  ok   does not join two characters across a long pause
  ok   chains through a correction, never across it
  ok   chains a hotstring's output and keeps its source
  ok   does not carry a word across a correction
  ok   flags the n-grams of the character a Backspace erases
  ok   erases nothing typed before a long pause

=== ngram walker: what the writer receives ===
  ok   splits the batch by table and by application-day
  ok   emits nothing for a family with no rows

=== ngram walker: a real flush writes every family ===
  ok   hands more than one table to the writer

=== ngram walker: each character is stored once ===
  ok   counts a typed character once in ngram_chars

=== keystats: a JSON summary cannot acknowledge raw SQLite history ===
  ok   retains the exact raw source while native persistence is unavailable

=== aggregate walker: what the day was made of ===
  ok   sorts characters into the five classes
  ok   counts an accented letter as a letter
  ok   does not count an expansion as something the user typed

=== aggregate walker: corrections ===
  ok   counts manual backspaces
  ok   does not count the deletions a hotstring makes to erase its trigger
  ok   counts a run of three or more as one cascade
  ok   does not call a single backspace a cascade
  ok   closes a cascade that is still open when the stream ends
  ok   measures how quickly the user resumed
  ok   does not call a coffee break recovery time

=== aggregate walker: when the typing happened ===
  ok   credits each keystroke to its hour and its five-minute slot
  ok   records the first and last five-minute slot the user typed in
  ok   skips the time-of-day tables rather than guessing when it has no clock

=== aggregate walker: runs of typing ===
  ok   counts an uninterrupted run as one burst
  ok   starts a new burst after a real gap
  ok   credits a burst still open when the stream ends
  ok   keeps the squared delays so rhythm is recoverable
  ok   records one session for a continuous stretch
  ok   splits sessions at the coarser threshold, not the burst one

=== aggregate walker: the pause buckets ===
  ok   credits a delay to every threshold at or above it
  ok   counts the keystrokes each bucket credits
  ok   unrolls one row per threshold for the writer

